# Deploy SSH key keeps disappearing (GCP VM)

- Date: 2026-11-09
- Where: GitHub Actions, `deploy` job → GCP VM

## Symptom

```
ssh: handshake failed: ssh: unable to authenticate, attempted methods [none publickey], no supported methods remain
```

I added the deploy public key to `~/.ssh/authorized_keys`, but it disappeared after a few minutes.

## Cause

GCP's Guest Agent manages `authorized_keys` using the SSH keys in the VM metadata.
When the metadata changes (for example, when the console SSH button adds or removes a temporary key), it rewrites the file and removes my key.

## Solution

Put the deploy key in a separate file and make SSH read both files.

```bash
echo 'ssh-ed25519 AAAA... github-actions-deploy' > ~/.ssh/authorized_keys_deploy
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/authorized_keys_deploy

echo 'AuthorizedKeysFile .ssh/authorized_keys .ssh/authorized_keys_deploy' \
  | sudo tee /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/10-deploy-keys.conf

sudo sshd -t
sudo systemctl reload ssh
```

## Verification

```bash
sudo sshd -T | grep -i authorizedkeysfile
# → authorizedkeysfile .ssh/authorized_keys .ssh/authorized_keys_deploy
```

## Lessons learned

If two programs manage the same file, give each one its own file.